Looking at the graph, the curve rises from the left, crosses the x-axis at x = -2, reaches its peak at the point (1, 4), then decreases, crossing the x-axis at x = 4.

The highest point of the curve (the peak of the parabola) occurs at x = 1, where the y-value is 4. Since the function changes from increasing to decreasing there, this peak gives the local maximum value.

\boxed{4}
